From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] vkd3d: no submission barrier command buffer on
 KosmicKrisp

vkd3d-proton appends a reusable SIMULTANEOUS_USE command buffer, one
full barrier (ALL_COMMANDS to ALL_COMMANDS and HOST), to every
ExecuteCommandLists submission, except on the drivers that sync host
readback on their own; those get a serializing binary semaphore instead.
Metal cannot resubmit a command buffer, so KosmicKrisp re-records that
barrier buffer into a new Metal command buffer on every submission, with
a residency pass, an allocation and the queue mutex, to commit a barrier
with nothing to order.

Add KosmicKrisp to that list. Its only memory type is host visible and
coherent, and a Metal command buffer's completion makes its writes
visible to the host, so the serializing semaphore keeps the order
and the host's view of GPU writes. Nothing else changes.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-08-vulkan-perf-vkd3d-kk-driver.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 libs/vkd3d/command.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/command.c b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
index ea1e8a0..9f3f5f0 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/command.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
@@ -111,7 +111,8 @@ static bool vkd3d_driver_implicitly_syncs_host_readback(VkDriverId driver_id)
     return driver_id == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_RADV ||
             driver_id == VK_DRIVER_ID_AMD_PROPRIETARY ||
             driver_id == VK_DRIVER_ID_AMD_OPEN_SOURCE ||
-            driver_id == VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY;
+            driver_id == VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY ||
+            driver_id == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_KOSMICKRISP;
 }
 
 HRESULT vkd3d_queue_create(struct d3d12_device *device, uint32_t family_index, uint32_t queue_index,
